		(uuid "360b05f4-0196-4d54-a7e3-c0421e8661fa")
	)
	(text "I2C is an open-drain protocol, the chip sends the zero\n by pulling the line low, hence pull-up resistors neeeded\n for I2C lines. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 31.75 365.506 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "596167cc-6917-4712-be91-630f955764d4")
	)
	(text "U7 is an open-drain buffer, \nit prevents the LED from pulling too much \ncurrent from the chip causing a voltage sag.\nIt does so by having a high-impedance input pin\nso no high current draw from the chip.\nU7 connects LED to ground to turn the LED on\nafter RESETZ is pulled low (0). "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 184.404 366.268 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "5d31e786-9797-4362-be2b-aea8c209590c")
	)
	(text "R7 is a current limiting resistor, \nacting as a pull-up for the open-drain \nbuffer at the same time I think. "
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 184.404 377.698 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "65ceaad9-61a6-43aa-8c1a-bd3e81c6c372")
	)
